User Story 1: Reinstating Defaulted Accounts
ID: SA-DIR-01
Priority: High
Risk: High
Estimate: 5 Story Points

Narrative: As a Director of Operations, I want to manually override the status of an account flagged as in default, so that a merchant can resume ordering after long-term debt issues are resolved.

Acceptance Criteria:
The system must restrict this functionality specifically to users with Director-level credentials.
The system must require a mandatory "reason for reinstatement" text entry before the status can be changed.
Upon execution, the merchant's status must change from "in default" to "normal" and the restriction on placing new orders must be lifted.
The system must log the Director's ID and timestamp the action for the annual audit trail.

User Story 2: Managing System-Wide Discount Plans
ID: SA-DIR-02
Priority: Medium
Risk: Medium
Estimate: 8 Story Points

Narrative: As a Director of Operations, I want to configure the parameters for fixed and flexible discount plans, so that the system automatically applies the correct pricing logic to merchant orders.

Acceptance Criteria:
The system must allow the Director to set the percentage for "Fixed" discounts applied to specific merchant categories.
The system must allow the definition of "Flexible" discount thresholds (e.g., 5% off for orders exceeding £1000).
The system must ensure that only one discount plan type can be active for a single merchant at any given time.
The updated logic must be immediately accessible to the order validation engine to ensure correct invoicing.

User Story 3: Global Turnover Reporting
ID: SA-DIR-03
Priority: Medium
Risk: Low
Estimate: 13 Story Points

Narrative: As a Director of Operations, I want to generate a high-level turnover report for the entire company, so that I can analyze total sales performance across all merchants and product categories.

Acceptance Criteria:
The report must aggregate total revenue from all successfully processed orders within a user-defined date range.
The system must provide a breakdown of turnover by product category (e.g., Antibiotics, Pain Relief).
The report must include a comparison between total invoiced amounts and total payments actually received.
The output must be generated in a high-level summary dashboard format with an option to download as a spreadsheet.

User Story 4: Advanced Product Search and Filtering
ID: SA-MER-01
Priority: High
Risk: Low
Estimate: 5 Story Points

Narrative: As a merchant, I want to search and filter the product catalogue by name and category, so that I can quickly find the pharmaceutical supplies I need to stock in my pharmacy.

Acceptance Criteria:
The system must allow keyword searches that match against the product name or description.
The interface must provide filters for "Package Type" (e.g., box, bottle, vial) and "Category."
The results must only display items that are currently marked as "active" in the staff catalogue.
The search must return results within one second to maintain a professional user experience.

User Story 5: Order Status and Tracking
ID: SA-MER-02
Priority: High
Risk: Low
Estimate: 5 Story Points

Narrative: As a merchant, I want to view the real-time status of my submitted orders, so that I can track when my supplies have been accepted, processed, or dispatched.

Acceptance Criteria:
The system must provide an "Order History" view where each order is tagged with its current state (Accepted, Processing, Dispatched, or Delivered).
For orders marked as "Dispatched," the system must display the courier name and the tracking number provided by the operations staff.
The merchant must be able to view a detailed breakdown of the items included in each historical order.
The system must display an "Invoiced" status once the financial department has confirmed the order totals.

User Story 6: Real-time Credit and Debt Overview
ID: SA-MER-03
Priority: High
Risk: Medium
Estimate: 3 Story Points

Narrative: As a merchant, I want to view my current outstanding debt and remaining credit limit, so that I can ensure I have sufficient funds to place a new order.

Acceptance Criteria:
The dashboard must clearly display three figures: Total Credit Limit, Current Outstanding Debt, and Available Credit.
The "Available Credit" must be a calculated field (Total Limit minus Current Debt).
The system must provide a warning if the merchant’s current debt is within 10% of their total limit.
The data must be pulled directly from the SA central database to ensure it reflects the most recent payments processed by the accounting staff.
